First, reflection is only necessary on Ludios if there is a
black dragon there (and even then, magic resistence will work as
well).  A quick check on first entering it should tell you
whether that is the case or not.  Beyond that: if you've not
max'ed out your divine protection, Ludios will generally allow
you to do so; and unless you've already got gloves which are
max'ed, just doing the start of Ludios (killing all of the
soldiers) will often give you some enchanted gloves.  And once
or twice, Ludios provided me with dragon scales (gray or
silver), so I didn't have to wish for them later.

> WRT Castle; either if I have MR, or if I have telepathy and no
> purple L's are there then I'd do the Castle. (Music
> instruments or levitation/jumping required for me. You can use
> a scroll of earth and striking/force bolt as well, but I
> dislike being swarmed by the monsters there.)

If you use the scrolls of earth to set up a nice corridor, you
won't be swarmed.  Not always possible, it depends somewhat on
the layout behind you.  But I've used this strategy more than
once successfully.

